1 TRUE POSITIVE: src/click/_termui_impl.py:596-604 (`Editor.edit_files`) — builds `args=f"{editor} {exc_filename}"` and passes it to `subprocess.Popen(..., shell=True)`. `exc_filename` is built by naively wrapping filenames in double quotes without escaping shell metacharacters/bare `"`, and `editor` comes from `Editor(editor=...)` or the VISUAL/EDITOR environment variables. Both `click.edit(filename=...)` and `Editor.edit()` (with a temp file) route into this sink, so a filename containing `$(...)`, backticks, or a `"` will be interpreted by the shell → arbitrary command execution (CWE-78). Exploitation requires the attacker to influence a filename passed to click.edit (e.g. an untrusted path/name edited by a CLI tool).

